Unpublished raw controller ABI retirement: historical inputs, not production.

Immediately removed:
- 101 obsolete ioctl declarations, their authorization membership and rejection
  dispatchers. Unknown encoded commands now reach ENOTTY before CAP, selection,
  Runtime lookup or usercopy. Old numbers remain reserved; current unsupported
  new modes keep their own explicit error contracts.
- Unused old Kernel C/Rust layouts and the old normalized public event codes.
  Current 26 controls and 27 C ABI structures retain their original numbers,
  fields, sizes and semantics. Native Host/Session/Grant/credit/Ticket unchanged.

Test-only witnesses:
- include/ and net/ preserve exact original4b6 source. dispatch.rs preserves the
  retired arms. ssap_permissions.h is the original permission helper, not a new
  SSAP implementation. Actual userspace permission types and Engine remain.
- test-migration-audit.json binds thirteen original suite/tool sources by hash.
  The old monolithic suite, raw Runtime/hotplug/USB terminal loops and old CLI
  are no longer default tests or recommended tools. Files are retained verbatim;
  their relative includes require their original source checkout for replay.
- retained-numbers.json comes from independently compiled pre-retirement
  x86_64/i386 declarations. retired_ioctl_numbers.h is test-only and never an
  alias to the new API. run_raw_uapi_retirement.py checks both targets and
  deliberate mutations. This is not actual ioctl or compatibility proof.

Current consumers and migration:
- run_virtual_vm.py uses retired_uapi_test.c: actual current file affinity and
  every101old encoding, buffer/NULL/invalid-user-address, ENOTTY and unchanged
  output. Root and uid1000, two rounds; new VM qualification is required.
- Native open/usercopy probes use native_runtime_probe.h with actual typed
  DiagnosticSubmit/Result, original generation/request/sequence/deadline and
  accounting checks. Shared generic QMP/artifact helpers are vm_test_utils.py.
- kernel_authorization_test.c tests12current privileged and12observational
  commands plus affinity; old101are ENOTTY even with inherited fds and no CAP.
  Retired configfs attributes must be absent; old PM models are not re-enabled.
- daemon management seed uses a real typed query and denies another author's
  retained result with EPERM. New slkconfig has no shared reply queue to drain.
- User VM bundle/caller, private cross-language history and CI pin migrate in
  the companion userspace change. Kernel build alone does not qualify them.

Waiting for replacement/acceptance:
- Migrate useful old synthetic USB terminal, repeated-reply/hotplug and bounded
  recovery cases to current typed requests before claiming new coverage. The
  current Virtual gate and preserved pure regressions do not cover the whole
  historical USB runner. Neither those historical models nor QMP/manual power
  cycles qualify natural fault recovery.
- Exact new full Kernel/normal and private-module boot, actual permissions and
  real WS73 short/boundary/long/Owned/security preservation gates remain needed.
- Full R5 AppSDK/CLI/C-Python/contracts and R6 clean-VM deployment remain open.

Authority: sparklink/project/implementation-plan.md WP18 R4f2e; K#6/#17/#19,
U#3/#6/#8. Full S0-S6/19WP/10FV/12DG and all original acceptance remain.
History or local compilation must never be relabelled current architecture,
formal, actual driver concurrency, RF or automatic recovery acceptance.
